    "['ipv6 unicast-routing', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static route ::/0 discard', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static route ::/0 discard', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset routing-options rib inet6.0 static route ::/0 discard\\n##\\n\\nNote: While the Juniper command doesn\\'t exactly mirror \"ipv6 unicast-routing\", it achieves the same functional purpose by enabling IPv6 routing capabilities. The Cisco command globally enables IPv6 routing, while the Juniper equivalent sets up the basic IPv6 routing infrastructure.\\n\\nFor a more direct equivalent, you could also use:\\n##\\nset system static-host-mapping inet6 enable\\n##\\nor\\n##\\nset routing-options autonomous-system 65000\\n##\\n\\nHowever, IPv6 routing is typically enabled by default in Junos, and the first command provided is the most practical equivalent configuration.', 'trans_template': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static route ::/0 discard'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system static-host-mapping inet6 enable', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system static-host-mapping inet6 enable', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset routing-options rib inet6.0 static route ::/0 discard\\n##\\n\\nNote: While the Juniper command doesn\\'t exactly mirror \"ipv6 unicast-routing\", it achieves the same functional purpose by enabling IPv6 routing capabilities. The Cisco command globally enables IPv6 routing, while the Juniper equivalent sets up the basic IPv6 routing infrastructure.\\n\\nFor a more direct equivalent, you could also use:\\n##\\nset system static-host-mapping inet6 enable\\n##\\nor\\n##\\nset routing-options autonomous-system 65000\\n##\\n\\nHowever, IPv6 routing is typically enabled by default in Junos, and the first command provided is the most practical equivalent configuration.', 'trans_template': 'set system static-host-mapping inet6 enable'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-options autonomous-system 65000', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set routing-options autonomous-system 65000', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset routing-options rib inet6.0 static route ::/0 discard\\n##\\n\\nNote: While the Juniper command doesn\\'t exactly mirror \"ipv6 unicast-routing\", it achieves the same functional purpose by enabling IPv6 routing capabilities. The Cisco command globally enables IPv6 routing, while the Juniper equivalent sets up the basic IPv6 routing infrastructure.\\n\\nFor a more direct equivalent, you could also use:\\n##\\nset system static-host-mapping inet6 enable\\n##\\nor\\n##\\nset routing-options autonomous-system 65000\\n##\\n\\nHowever, IPv6 routing is typically enabled by default in Junos, and the first command provided is the most practical equivalent configuration.', 'trans_template': 'set routing-options autonomous-system 65000'}]]": 1,
