    "['ipv6 router [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `ipv6 router isis` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, you enable IS-IS on an interface through the protocols hierarchy\\n- The interface name is translated to Juniper's naming convention (ge-1/0/1)\\n- Juniper requires the logical unit number (here .0 is used as default)\\n- Unlike Cisco where IPv6 IS-IS is configured under the interface, Juniper automatically handles both IPv4 and IPv6 IS-IS when enabled on an interface\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0'}]]": 1,
